1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,150
The most important penalty of his life…

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:04,250
…and he chipped it down the middle.

3
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:07,950
June 20, 1976. Belgrade.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,950
The European Championship final.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,250
Czechoslovakia against West Germany.

6
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:14,250
2–2 after extra time.

7
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:17,800
For the first time, a European final goes to penalties.

8
00:00:17,850 --> 00:00:20,550
7 kicks. 7 goals.

9
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:24,850
Then… Uli Hoeness blasts West Germany’s fourth… over the bar.

10
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:26,750
Antonín Panenka steps up.

11
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:29,750
Score this, and Czechoslovakia are champions.

12
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:33,150
In goal: World Cup winner Sepp Maier.

13
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:36,150
Panenka runs in… Maier dives to his left…

14
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:39,750
…and Panenka chips it, softly, into the middle.

15
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:41,650
He practised it after training,

16
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:46,050
betting his club’s goalkeeper a beer or a chocolate bar on every kick.

17
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:48,450
Today, that penalty has a name.

18
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:50,250
A Panenka.

19
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:51,450
Would you dare to take it?

20
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:53,150
Tell me in the comments.
